# SQL Number Functions

## 📌 What are Number Functions?

**Number Functions** are built-in SQL functions used to perform mathematical operations on numeric values.

These functions help in calculations, rounding, finding absolute values, powers, square roots, and more.

---

# Common SQL Number Functions

| Function | Description |
|----------|-------------|
| ABS() | Returns the absolute value |
| CEIL() / CEILING() | Rounds up to the nearest integer |
| FLOOR() | Rounds down to the nearest integer |
| ROUND() | Rounds a number |
| TRUNCATE() | Truncates decimal places |
| MOD() | Returns remainder |
| POWER() | Returns a number raised to a power |
| SQRT() | Returns square root |
| RAND() | Generates a random number |
| SIGN() | Returns sign of a number |

---

